IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`

-- g6-notice-and-hearing.l4: ss.42-44.  The notice of intention and what it must state (s.42), the right to
-- make representations within 30 days (s.43), the Commissioner's decision, the payment demand and the notice
-- of a decision not to impose (s.44(a) to (c)), and the notice treated as a payment demand (s.44(d)).
--
-- Clock convention for every regulative rule that carries a WITHIN in this module: `AT 0` is the day the
-- period runs from (the day the notice was delivered), and an event `AT k` happened k days after it.  The
-- WITHIN is the number of days from that day to the last day of the period, computed by the vendored
-- time module (Interpretation Law s.10); the last day is inside the period, as an act AT the WITHIN is timely.
--
-- Periods owned here (PLAN section (d)):
--   P26, s.43: 30 days from delivery of the notice: a window in which a representation may be made, kind W.
--     IL s.10(a), and IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4); the alternative without s.10(c) is callable.
--   P27, s.44(d): "at the end of that period": kind C.  The date is the last day of the s.43 period; IL s.10(c)
--     is not applied a second time by this rule; a reading that counts from the day after is callable.
--
-- Not in the sources: how a document is delivered; whether the Commissioner may extend the s.43 period after
-- it has run; any time limit for giving the notice of intention or for the Commissioner's decision.

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter A: imposing a financial sanction`

§§§ `ss 42 to 44: the acts`

@desc The acts of ss.42 to 44: giving the notice of intention, making representations, extending the period, deciding, and giving the payment demand or the notice of no sanction; the first field says who performs each act
DECLARE `Act under ss 42 to 44` IS ONE OF
    `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction`
        HAS `performed by the notifying officer` IS A Party
            `the notice given` IS A `Notice of intention`
    `make written representations to the Commissioner`
        HAS `performed by the representing violator` IS A Party
    `extend the period for representations`
        HAS `performed by the extending officer` IS A Party
            `the extension granted` IS AN `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
    `decide whether to impose a financial sanction`
        HAS `performed by the deciding officer` IS A Party
            `the decision taken` IS A `Decision on a financial sanction`
    `give the violator a payment demand`
        HAS `performed by the demanding officer` IS A Party
            `the demand given` IS A `Payment demand`
    `give the violator written notice that no financial sanction is imposed`
        HAS `performed by the officer giving notice of no sanction` IS A Party
            `the notice given of no sanction` IS A `Notice of a decision not to impose a sanction`

§§§ `A helper: the calendar of rest days as the predicate the time module takes`

-- Days of rest, recess or holiday are an INPUT (a list of dates), never computed.
GIVEN calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar MEANS
    `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`)

-- The later of two days: an extension that ends before the standard 30 days are out does not shorten them (s.43 and
-- s.53(b) allow the Commissioner to EXTEND the period; fork F-SHORTEN).
GIVEN one IS A DATE
      other IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Chapter 6 — the later of` one `and` other MEANS
    IF   one AT LEAST other
    THEN one
    ELSE other

§§§ `s 42: notice of intention to impose a financial sanction`

-- src:346 | {{ח:סעיף|42|הודעה על כוונת חיוב}}
-- src:347 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} היה לממונה יסוד סביר להניח כי אדם הפר הוראה מההוראות לפי חוק זה, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 41|בסעיף 41}} ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} – המפר), ובכוונתו להטיל עליו עיצום כספי לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}}, ימסור למפר הודעה בכתב על הכוונה להטיל עליו עיצום כספי ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} – הודעה על כוונת חיוב).
-- s.42(a): "If the Commissioner had reasonable grounds to think a person breached a provision ... and he intends
-- to impose a financial sanction on him, he shall deliver to the violator a written notice of the intention".
-- The grounds and the intention are the Commissioner's: inputs.  No time limit is stated, so no WITHIN: the
-- duty stands until performed.  The guard rejects a notice that omits what (b) requires.
@ref s.42(a) (src:347)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 42(a) — the Commissioner must give notice of intention` `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction` `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` MEANS
    IF       `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act`
         AND `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision`
         AND `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction` `the Commissioner` notice
               PROVIDED `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:348 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} בהודעה על כוונת חיוב יציין הממונה, בין השאר, את אלה:
-- src:349 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} המעשה או המחדל ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} – המעשה), המהווה את ההפרה ומועד ביצוע ההפרה;
-- src:350 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} סכום העיצום הכספי והתקופה לתשלומו;
-- src:351 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} זכותו של המפר לטעון את טענותיו לפני הממונה לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 43|סעיף 43}} וכי יראו את ההודעה על כוונת חיוב כדרישת תשלום אם המפר לא יממש את הזכות האמורה, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 44|בסעיף 44(ד)}};
-- src:352 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} הסמכות להוסיף על סכום העיצום הכספי בשל הפרה נמשכת או הפרה חוזרת לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 45|סעיף 45}}, ושיעור התוספת.
-- The contents (b)(1) to (4) are the limbs a notice must state, "among other things" ("ben hashe'ar"), so the
-- list is a minimum, not a closed list.  A notice that does not state them is not "a notice under s.42": s.43
-- gives the right of representation to a violator "to whom a notice of intention was delivered under s.42",
-- and s.44(d) deems the NOTICE a payment demand.  That is a reading (fork F-NOTICE in FRAGMENT-G6.md).
@ref s.42(b) (src:348-352)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice MEANS
        "(a) written notice" ... notice's `in writing`
    ... "(b)(1)" ... notice's `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach`
    ... "(b)(2) the amount" ... notice's `states the amount of the sanction`
    ... "(b)(2) the period for payment" ... isJust (notice's `the period for payment the notice states, in days`)
    ... "(b)(3) the right to make representations" ... notice's `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43`
    ... "(b)(3) the notice treated as a payment demand" ... notice's `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used`
    AND "(b)(4)" ... notice's `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition`

§§§ `s 43: the right to make representations, 30 days from delivery of the notice`

-- src:354 | {{ח:סעיף|43|זכות טיעון}}
-- src:355 | {{ח:ת}} מפר שנמסרה לו הודעה על כוונת חיוב לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 42|סעיף 42}}, רשאי לטעון את טענותיו, בכתב, לפני הממונה, לעניין הכוונה להטיל עליו עיצום כספי ולעניין סכומו, בתוך 30 ימים ממועד מסירת ההודעה; הממונה רשאי להאריך את התקופה האמורה, מטעמים מיוחדים שיירשמו.
-- The 30 days, kind W (a window in which a person may act): IL s.10(a), the day of delivery not counted, and
-- IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4), so a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday moves to the next day
-- that is not one.  The alternative without s.10(c) follows.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` delivered calendar MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` delivered `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice, without s 10(c)` delivered MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` delivered

-- "the Commissioner may extend the said period, for special reasons that shall be recorded": the extension is
-- an official's choice of a day (kind X: an input, never computed).  An extension without recorded reasons is
-- not the extension the section allows, and is ignored (fork F-EXT).
@ref s.43 (src:355)
@export The last day on which a violator may make written representations after a notice of intention: 30 days from its delivery, moved past days of rest, recess or holiday, or the day an extension granted for recorded special reasons ends when that is later
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention` @desc The notice of intention to impose a financial sanction: when it was delivered and what it states
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner` @desc The extension the Commissioner granted, if any: the day the period now ends and whether special reasons were recorded; NOTHING if none was granted
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under an enactment for the years the question touches, as a list of dates (never computed)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER extension
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (notice's `delivered on`) calendar
    WHEN JUST granted THEN
        IF   granted's `special reasons were recorded`
        THEN `Chapter 6 — the later of` (granted's `the period now ends on`) `and` (`s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (notice's `delivered on`) calendar)
        ELSE `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (notice's `delivered on`) calendar

-- Fork F-SHORTEN: the extension is the period's end whatever day the Commissioner chose, even one before the 30 days
-- are out.  The reading taken is that "extend" cannot shorten, so the 30 days stand.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day for representations, an extension that ends before the 30 days being taken as it is` notice extension calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER extension
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (notice's `delivered on`) calendar
    WHEN JUST granted THEN
        IF   granted's `special reasons were recorded`
        THEN granted's `the period now ends on`
        ELSE `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice` (notice's `delivered on`) calendar

-- Fork F-EXT: an extension counts whether or not reasons were recorded (the standard end here is without s.10(c), so the
-- alternative differs from the reading taken in both ways; an extension that ends earlier than the 30 days still does not
-- shorten them).
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day for representations, without s 10(c) and counting an extension whether or not reasons were recorded` notice extension MEANS
    CONSIDER extension
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice, without s 10(c)` (notice's `delivered on`)
    WHEN JUST granted THEN `Chapter 6 — the later of` (granted's `the period now ends on`) `and` (`s 43 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the notice, without s 10(c)` (notice's `delivered on`))

-- The alternative that applies IL s.10(c) to an extension too (forks F-X and F-C): an official's chosen day is moved past
-- days of rest, recess or holiday like any other last day.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 43 — the last day for representations, with s 10(c) applied to an extension as well` notice extension calendar MEANS
    `s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` (`s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

-- Is a day timely, within the s.43 period?  Representations made on the day the notice is delivered are "within 30 days
-- from" it: IL s.10(a) leaves the day of delivery out of the COUNT that fixes the last day, it does not make an act on
-- that day untimely (fork F-ACTDAY).  So a day is timely when it is the day of delivery or later, and the last day or
-- earlier; the last day is inside.  A day before the notice was delivered is not.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43 — the day` day `is within the period for representations of` notice extension calendar MEANS
        (notice's `delivered on` AT MOST day)
    AND (day AT MOST `s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)

-- Fork F-ACTDAY: the strict reading, the period beginning the day AFTER delivery, so an act on the day of delivery is
-- not within it.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` day `is within the period for representations of` notice extension calendar MEANS
    `s 8, s 10 — the date` day `is inside the period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (notice's `delivered on`)) `and ending on` (`s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)

-- The number of days from the day of delivery (AT 0) to the last day: the WITHIN of the right below.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 43 — the number of days from the day of delivery to the last day for representations` notice extension calendar MEANS
    (Day (`s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)) MINUS (Day (notice's `delivered on`))

-- Did the violator make his representations within the period?  s.44(d) turns on whether he did not.  A day inside the
-- period is one on which he may; NOTHING is a violator who has made none.
@ref s.43, s.44(d) (src:355, src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `the day the violator made his representations` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` notice extension calendar `the day the violator made his representations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the violator made his representations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST day THEN `s 43 — the day` day `is within the period for representations of` notice extension calendar

-- Fork F-ACTDAY: with the period beginning the day after delivery, representations made on the day of delivery are late.
@ref s.43, s.44(d) (src:355, src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `the day the violator made his representations` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 43, s 44(d) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the violator made his representations within the period` notice extension calendar `the day the violator made his representations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the violator made his representations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST day THEN `s 43 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` day `is within the period for representations of` notice extension calendar

-- The right: the violator MAY make written representations, about the intention and the amount, within the
-- period.  The WITHIN is the whole number of days from the day of delivery (AT 0) to the last day.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 43 — the violator may make written representations` notice extension calendar MEANS
    IF   `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
    THEN PARTY  `the violator`
         MAY    `make written representations to the Commissioner` `the violator`
         WITHIN (`s 43 — the number of days from the day of delivery to the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The alternative that gives the right whatever the notice states (fork F-NOTICE): a notice that omits what s.42(b)
-- requires still starts the 30 days.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 43 — the violator may make written representations, whatever the notice states` notice extension calendar MEANS
    PARTY  `the violator`
    MAY    `make written representations to the Commissioner` `the violator`
    WITHIN (`s 43 — the number of days from the day of delivery to the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)

-- The power to extend: the Commissioner MAY, if he finds special reasons, which he must record.
@ref s.43 (src:355)
GIVEN `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 43 — the Commissioner may extend the period for representations` `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension` MEANS
    IF   `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `extend the period for representations` `the Commissioner` granted
               PROVIDED granted's `special reasons were recorded`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `s 44: the Commissioner's decision and the payment demand`

-- src:357 | {{ח:סעיף|44|החלטת הממונה ודרישת תשלום}}
-- src:358 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הממונה יחליט, לאחר ששקל את הטענות שנטענו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 43|סעיף 43}}, אם להטיל על המפר עיצום כספי, ורשאי הוא להפחית את סכום העיצום הכספי לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 46|סעיף 46}}.
-- (a): the Commissioner decides, after considering the representations made under s.43, whether to impose a
-- sanction.  The decision is his discretion: an input.  If no representations were made within the period, (d)
-- applies instead and there is nothing to decide.
@ref s.44(a) (src:358)
GIVEN `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      decision IS A `Decision on a financial sanction`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 44(a) — the Commissioner decides after representations` `representations were made within the period` decision MEANS
    IF   `representations were made within the period`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `decide whether to impose a financial sanction` `the Commissioner` decision
         HENCE `s 44(b) — what the Commissioner must give the violator after deciding` decision
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:359 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} החליט הממונה לפי הוראות סעיף קטן (א) –
-- src:360 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} להטיל על המפר עיצום כספי – ימסור לו דרישה, בכתב, לשלם את העיצום הכספי ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} – דרישת תשלום), שבה יציין, בין השאר, את סכום העיצום הכספי המעודכן ואת התקופה לתשלומו;
-- src:361 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} שלא להטיל על המפר עיצום כספי – ימסור לו הודעה על כך, בכתב.
-- (b): after deciding under (a), the Commissioner must give the violator a written demand (if he decided to
-- impose) or a written notice (if not).  No time limit is stated, so no WITHIN.
@ref s.44(b) (src:359-361)
GIVEN decision IS A `Decision on a financial sanction`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 42 to 44`
`s 44(b) — what the Commissioner must give the violator after deciding` decision MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `to impose the financial sanction` THEN
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        MUST  `give the violator a payment demand` `the Commissioner` demand
              PROVIDED `s 44(b)(1) and (c) — the payment demand states what the Law requires` demand
    WHEN `not to impose a financial sanction` THEN
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        MUST  `give the violator written notice that no financial sanction is imposed` `the Commissioner` notice
              PROVIDED `s 44(b)(2) and (c) — the notice of no sanction states what the Law requires` notice

-- src:362 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} בדרישת התשלום או בהודעה לפי סעיף קטן (ב) יפרט הממונה את נימוקי החלטתו.
-- (c): "in the payment demand or in the notice under (b) the Commissioner shall detail the reasons".  The
-- demand states, among other things, the updated amount and the period for payment (b)(1).
@ref s.44(b)(1), s.44(c) (src:360, src:362)
GIVEN demand IS A `Payment demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(b)(1) and (c) — the payment demand states what the Law requires` demand MEANS
        "(b)(1) in writing" ... demand's `in writing`
    ... "(b)(1) the updated amount" ... demand's `states the updated amount of the sanction`
    ... "(b)(1) the period for payment" ... isJust (demand's `the period for payment the demand states, in days`)
    AND "(c) the reasons" ... demand's `states the reasons for the decision`

@ref s.44(b)(2), s.44(c) (src:361-362)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of a decision not to impose a sanction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(b)(2) and (c) — the notice of no sanction states what the Law requires` notice MEANS
        "(b)(2) in writing" ... notice's `in writing`
    AND "(c) the reasons" ... notice's `states the reasons for the decision`

§§§ `s 44(d): a notice of intention that is treated as a payment demand`

-- src:363 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} לא טען המפר את טענותיו לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 43|סעיף 43}}, בתוך התקופה האמורה {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 43|באותו סעיף}}, יראו את ההודעה על כוונת חיוב, בתום אותה תקופה, כדרישת תשלום שנמסרה למפר במועד האמור.
-- "If the violator did not make his representations within the period said in that section, the notice of
-- intention shall be treated, at the end of that period, as a payment demand delivered to the violator on the
-- said date."  Kind C: a date counted from another date.  The period is the s.43 period, extension included
-- ("the said period" is the period s.43 allows, and s.43 lets the Commissioner extend it).  The date taken is
-- the LAST DAY of that period (the period ends on a day, and that day is inside it): so the deemed demand is
-- delivered on the day the 30 days end, and s.48's 30 days run from it (trap T16, forks F-DEEMED).  IL s.10(c)
-- is not applied a second time here: the date is the end of the s.43 period, which already has the s.10(c)
-- reading of kind W.  The reading from the day after the last day is callable below.
@ref s.44(d) (src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` notice extension calendar MEANS
    `s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar

@ref s.44(d) (src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered, counting from the day after the period ends` notice extension calendar MEANS
    `s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (`s 43 — the last day for representations` notice extension calendar)

-- The third reading of "the said date" (fork F-DEEMED): the date said earlier in the Law's text, the day the notice of
-- intention was delivered, so that the notice is treated as a demand delivered on the day it was in fact delivered.
@ref s.44(d) (src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered, the said date being the day the notice was delivered` notice MEANS
    notice's `delivered on`

@ref s.44(d) (src:363)
GIVEN `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(d) — the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand` `representations were made within the period` MEANS
    NOT `representations were made within the period`

-- Fork F-NOTICE, read through to s.44(d): a notice that omits what s.42(b) requires is not "a notice under s.42", so
-- it is no notice that s.44(d) can treat as a payment demand; the violator it was delivered to had no s.43 right to lose.
@ref s.42(b), s.44(d) (src:348-352, src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(d) — the notice` notice `is treated as a payment demand, given` `representations were made within the period` MEANS
        `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
    AND NOT `representations were made within the period`

-- The day the payment demand counts as delivered, for a violator who made representations (the demand's own
-- day, once there is one) and for one who did not (the s.44(d) day).  NOTHING: a violator who made
-- representations has not yet been given a demand.  NOTHING also for a violator who made none but whose notice omits
-- what s.42(b) requires: that is no notice under s.42 on the reading taken (fork F-NOTICE), so there is nothing for
-- s.44(d) to treat as a demand.
@ref s.44(b)(1), s.44(d) (src:360, src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      demand IS A MAYBE `Payment demand`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` notice extension `representations were made within the period` demand calendar MEANS
    IF   `representations were made within the period`
    THEN CONSIDER demand
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST given THEN JUST (given's `delivered on`)
    ELSE IF   `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
         THEN JUST (`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` notice extension calendar)
         ELSE NOTHING

-- Fork F-NOTICE: the other reading, a notice that omits what s.42(b) requires still starts the 30 days and is still
-- treated as a payment demand when no representations were made.
@ref s.44(b)(1), s.44(d) (src:360, src:363)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of intention`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      demand IS A MAYBE `Payment demand`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered, whatever the notice states` notice extension `representations were made within the period` demand calendar MEANS
    IF   `representations were made within the period`
    THEN CONSIDER demand
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST given THEN JUST (given's `delivered on`)
    ELSE JUST (`s 44(d) — the day the notice of intention is treated as a payment demand delivered` notice extension calendar)
